@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Monitoring in DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Monitoring is a crucial aspect of DevOps, allowing teams to track application performance, detect issues early, and ensure smooth operations in production environments.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why is Monitoring Important in DevOps?</h2>
        <p>DevOps relies on continuous monitoring to maintain system reliability and performance. Some key benefits include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Early Issue Detection:</strong> Identify and resolve problems before they impact users.</li>
            <li><strong>Improved Performance:</strong> Optimize resource usage and application responsiveness.</li>
            <li><strong>Enhanced Security:</strong> Monitor for suspicious activity and potential security breaches.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated Alerts:</strong> Set up notifications for performance issues and system failures.</li>
            <li><strong>Reduced Downtime:</strong> Proactive monitoring minimizes disruptions by identifying risks early.</li>
            <li><strong>Operational Insights:</strong> Data-driven monitoring helps teams make informed decisions.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/monitoring/media/monitoring-overview.png" alt="Monitoring in DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Real-time monitoring in DevOps</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Key Monitoring Tools in DevOps</h3>
        <p>Various tools help monitor applications and infrastructure in a DevOps pipeline. Some of the most popular ones include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Azure Monitor:</strong> Collects and analyzes telemetry data from Azure resources.</li>
            <li><strong>Application Insights:</strong> Provides application performance monitoring (APM) for .NET, Java, and Node.js applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Log Analytics:</strong> Helps collect and analyze logs for troubleshooting and insights.</li>
            <li><strong>Prometheus & Grafana:</strong> Open-source monitoring solutions widely used for Kubernetes and containerized applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Elastic Stack (ELK):</strong> A combination of Elasticsearch, Logstash, and Kibana used for log aggregation and analysis.</li>
            <li><strong>Datadog:</strong> Provides full-stack observability across applications, infrastructure, and logs.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Types of Monitoring in DevOps</h3>
        <p>Monitoring in DevOps can be categorized into different types:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Infrastructure Monitoring:</strong> Monitors servers, virtual machines, and cloud instances.</li>
            <li><strong>Application Performance Monitoring (APM):</strong> Tracks application responsiveness and reliability.</li>
            <li><strong>Log Monitoring:</strong> Collects and analyzes logs from different components.</li>
            <li><strong>Security Monitoring:</strong> Detects vulnerabilities and unauthorized activities.</li>
            <li><strong>Network Monitoring:</strong> Observes network traffic and connectivity issues.</li>
            <li><strong>End-User Experience Monitoring:</strong> Measures the impact of applications on user interactions.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Setting Up Monitoring in Azure DevOps</h3>
        <p>Follow these steps to enable monitoring for your applications and infrastructure:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Enable Azure Monitor:</strong> Go to Azure Portal > Monitor > Create a monitoring workspace.</li>
            <li><strong>Integrate Application Insights:</strong> Add the Application Insights SDK to your application and configure telemetry collection.</li>
            <li><strong>Configure Log Analytics:</strong> Set up log collection for virtual machines, containers, and applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Set Up Alerts:</strong> Define custom alerts to notify teams when issues arise.</li>
            <li><strong>Establish Dashboards:</strong> Use Grafana, Azure Monitor, or Kibana to visualize real-time metrics.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Incident Response:</strong> Integrate with tools like PagerDuty or Microsoft Teams for proactive issue resolution.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for Monitoring Integration</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: AzureMonitorAlerts@1
  inputs:
    azureSubscription: 'MyAzureSubscription'
    resourceGroupName: 'MyResourceGroup'
    alertRuleName: 'HighCPUAlert'
    conditionOperator: 'GreaterThan'
    conditionThreshold: '80'
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Monitoring in DevOps</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Monitor Across Environments:</strong> Ensure all stages (Dev, Test, Production) have monitoring enabled.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Incident Response:</strong> Use alerts and auto-remediation to minimize downtime.</li>
            <li><strong>Visualize Metrics:</strong> Use dashboards to track performance trends and anomalies.</li>
            <li><strong>Review Logs Regularly:</strong> Continuously analyze logs to detect patterns and security threats.</li>
            <li><strong>Establish SLAs and SLOs:</strong> Define service level agreements (SLAs) and objectives (SLOs) for performance measurement.</li>
            <li><strong>Enable Real-Time Alerting:</strong> Configure alerts to trigger based on threshold breaches.</li>
            <li><strong>Leverage AI and Machine Learning:</strong> Use predictive analytics to detect anomalies before they cause failures.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>By integrating monitoring into the DevOps workflow, teams can proactively detect issues, enhance performance, and improve user experience. Monitoring is essential for achieving high system availability and reliability.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("AzureMonitorInsights", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Azure Monitor & Application Insights &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>